#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:5
#: 8e82ef830c4f438c9ee23ef7e3a36e54
msgid "VTOL QUICKTUNE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:9
#: e3137f9fb59d402c8421ef0cfb8720bf
msgid "ArduPlane provides a quick means of obtaining a good tune for Quadplanes in VTOL modes. The process slowly increases the relevant gains until it detects an oscillation.  It then reduces the gains by 60% and moves onto the next gain. Once all the gains have been tuned the tune completes and the user can decide to save or discard the new gains."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:11
#: 91c52c856d8c4e07a28aa1f15aa16cad
msgid "be sure that you have prepared the vehicle for tuning by setting up parameters discussed here: :ref:`quadplane-vtol-tuning-process` Steps 1 to 11 and then use this mechanism in Step 12. Also to assure the best tune, setup the noise notch filtering, see :ref:`common-imu-notch-filtering`. You may run QUICKTUNE without this step to obtain initial fine tune, see :ref:`ac_rollpitchtuning` if the vehicle can't do an initial hover stably. Then setup the filters and retune for best results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:13
#: 04b3f685553745b39d6bd526fc5ab891
msgid "The script attempts to automatically tune the P/I and D gain of each axis enabled for tuning when an two or three position RC switch, whose ``RCx_OPTION`` is \"181\", is moved to the \"tune\" position. It will, by default, also adjust some PID loop filter values based on the :ref:`INS_GYRO_FILTER<INS_GYRO_FILTER>` setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:15
#: 2b890b1e022f43d0be0029c07ad41353
msgid "The advantage over QAUTOTUNE is that QUICKTUNE is safer because the vehicle does not need to move or twitch and QAUTOTUNE can occasionally result in instablity. Therefore QAUTOTUNE is not longer recommended for use, except by experts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:17
#: 4ef90cd1d6194f4ca665eb0b1e3b7896
msgid "The disadvantage is that QUICKTUNE cannot find the vehicle's maximum rotational accelerations or tune the attitude angle outer loops from their default or pre-tune adjusted (:ref:`quadplane-vtol-tuning-process`) values. However, tuning only the inner rate loops usually will yield a stable, safe flying vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:20
#: 99e01e2f7964490398131d6c0fe2bdbd
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:21
#: 70c278ade551492480b71fdd5f6dca04
msgid "Set :ref:`QWIK_ENABLE<QWIK_ENABLE>` = \"1\" to enable QUICKTUNE."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:22
#: f46d06a82ab14e4ebb06921cbbc1c352
msgid "Set :ref:`QWIK_AXES<QWIK_AXES>` to which axes (Roll/Pitch/Yaw)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:25
#: 23a135e828d14ae79d9acb51c96f0531
msgid "Activation RC Switch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:26
#: a690759ae31e4a0ebe75de32bcb9c250
msgid "Set up a two or three position RC switch with ``RCx_OPTION`` = \"181\". If it is a two position switch set :ref:`QWIK_OPTIONS<QWIK_OPTIONS>` bit 0 to \"1\", and you probably want to set the :ref:`QWIK_AUTO_SAVE<QWIK_AUTO_SAVE>` parameter to autosave the tune once completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:28
#: ad79b23363d7475ea57b757d283f32c1
msgid "With a three position switch, moving the switch to \"high\" (>1800us) is the \"save\" position which will save the current tune parameters, even if the tune is not completed yet. Moving the switch to the middle position activates the tuning process (\"tune\"). Moving the switch to the \"low\" position (<1200us), stops the tuning and reverts the parameters to their values before tuning began."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:30
#: 58ea2ecf109e438cbeacc48600977ca1
msgid "RC AUX switches only operate on transitions of the switch. Their position at boot does nothing, so if a switch is \"high\" at boot, in order to get the \"high\" function, it must be moved to another position and then back \"high\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:32
#: 52fee9d2b0524b5ebd578c306fbbd548
msgid "With a two position switch, \"high\" is the \"tune\" position, and \"low\" stops/reverts tuning. In order to save parameters, you must have set the :ref:`QWIK_AUTO_SAVE<QWIK_AUTO_SAVE>` parameter or use a GCS AUX switch facility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:35
#: c7ac3208b0cb46dfbba8c790a4aacda1
msgid "Tuning Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:36
#: d70a39e80d04436595e0ae5202fef64d
msgid "Wait for a calm day and go to an open area with good GPS reception"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:37
#: 424375c233794b05ad05a60bd43022a2
msgid "Use an OSD, TX OSD (using :ref:`Yaapu <common-frsky-yaapu>`), or GCS. This is where output from the tune will appear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:38
#: 424e3dd9f7c1434eb0dad6d72dbc472d
msgid "Move the RC switch to the low position OR push MP's Aux Function's \"Low\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:39
#: 28c883e797e84a47a0b83fbb70aa1ac3
msgid "Arm and takeoff in QLOITER mode and climb to a height of about 3m"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:40
#: d5ee41aff8a34a338f482fc2b33da8eb
msgid "Begin the tune by moving the RC switch to the \"tune\" position OR push MP's Aux Function's \"Mid\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:41
#: c765b83493014d8197c4818cc5b31414
msgid "Monitor the progress of the tune using the GCS's Messages tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:42
#: 6a07b771dc254398becd668244116c39
msgid "If necessary reposition the vehicle using the RC transmitter.  This will temporarily pause tuning.  Tuning will resume a few seconds after the RC sticks are returned to their center position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:43
#: 4e6497cb57434568b554687f9bb985f9
msgid "If the vehicle begins oscillating violently you can cancel the tune by moving the RC switch to the low position OR push MP's Aux Function's \"Low\" button. If the vehicle rocks or pitches more than :ref:`QWIK_ANGLE_MAX<QWIK_ANGLE_MAX>` the tune will automatically abort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quicktune.rst:44
#: 519b61539ba840f699c26438d77d7bf9
msgid "Once the tune has completed accept the new gains by moving the RC aux switch to the \"save\" position, wait for the :ref:`QWIK_AUTO_SAVE<QWIK_AUTO_SAVE>` timeout, OR push MP's Aux Function's \"High\" button"
msgstr ""

